## Prediction And Experiment Design
P1 seam-deletion invariance: deleting the two max-delta seam gates
should leave q=14V phase routing unchanged, as observed above.
P2 bypass-channel sensitivity: deleting the lower-delta same-component
bypass gates should move exactly 12 witnesses from gate-hit to no-gate
unless a wider gate basis adds a secondary channel.
P3 carry-lift stress: perturb or lift seam owners by C=27 classes;
preserving the endpoint mod-14 pair (1,9) should keep the seam/bypass
split more often than preserving raw owner size or raw delta.
P4 puncture filling: compare HYP-3478 singleton pockets against
random031's four punctures; isolated dead islands should be harmless
until a seven-owner seam connects their surrounding flow components.

